Spec: Shapes Module

Purpose:
  Shape models, creation tools, editing tools, and undoable commands
  for all vector geometry in the editor.

Structure:
  ./models: Shape class implementations (PathShape, TextObject, GroupShape, PathNode)
  ./tools: Interactive tools (select, pen, node-edit, text, fillet, offset)
  ./commands: Undoable command classes for all shape operations
  ./utils: Shared utilities (snapshot capture/restore)
  ./types.ts: Core IShape interface and type definitions

Owns:
  ./models/**
  ./tools/**
  ./commands/**
  ./utils/**
  ./types.ts

Must:
  All shapes implement the IShape interface.
  All shape modifications go through Command classes for undo/redo.
  Shape models provide clone(), getBounds(), toJSON(), and fromJSON().
  PathNode stores anchor position and two Bézier control handles.
  Tools extend BaseTool and implement onMouseDown/Move/Up lifecycle.

Must not:
  Directly mutate the Zustand store without going through setShapes().
  Skip the Command pattern for user-initiated changes.
  Import from ../ui or ../persistence (dependency direction is inward).

Depends on:
  @IShape interface
  @PathNode model
  @HistoryManager
  @useStore (Zustand)
  paper.js (for boolean and offset operations)
